   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🧠 Multimodal Deep Learning Master Tutorial: Vision, Language & Multi-Fusion Architectures\n",
    "\n",
    "Welcome to the **Multimodal Deep Learning** master tutorial using **PyTorch**, **NumPy**, and **Matplotlib**.\n",
    "\n",
    "--- \n",
    "## 🔰 Beginner's Guide & Key Concepts\n",
    "\n",
    "### What is Multimodal AI?\n",
    "Traditional AI models operate on a **single modality** (unimodal)—for instance, an image classifier processes only raw pixels, while a text classifier processes only sentences. **Multimodal AI models** integrate multiple data types—such as **Vision (Images)**, **Language (Text)**, and **Audio**—into a single neural network architecture to make holistic decisions.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Real-World Analogy 🧑‍⚕️\n",
    "- **Unimodal AI**: A doctor looking *only* at an X-ray picture.\n",
    "- **Multimodal AI**: A doctor looking at the **X-ray picture** + reading the **patient history report** + analyzing **blood test numbers**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Terminology:\n",
    "1. **Image Feature Vector**: Numerical representation of visual patterns extracted by a Vision model (e.g. ResNet or Vision Transformer, shape `[batch, 64]`).\n",
    "2. **Text Embedding**: Vector representing words or sentence context extracted by a Language model (e.g. BERT or Transformer encoder, shape `[batch, 128]`).\n",
    "3. **Feature Fusion**: Joining tensors using operations like concatenation (`torch.cat`), element-wise multiplication, or Cross-Attention so the network learns joint correlations.\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🚀 Quickstart: 5-Line PyTorch Multimodal Fusion\n",
    "Here is how multimodal feature fusion works in PyTorch in 5 simple lines:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# === 5-LINE BEGINNER PYTORCH FUSION DEMO ===\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "\n",
    "image_vector = torch.randn(1, 64)    # 1 sample with 64 vision features\n",
    "text_vector = torch.randn(1, 128)    # 1 sample with 128 text features\n",
    "\n",
    "# Fuse (Join) image + text features into a single combined vector along dim=1\n",
    "fused_vector = torch.cat((image_vector, text_vector), dim=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Simple Fusion Completed! Joined Vector Shape: {fused_vector.shape}\") # Output: [1, 192]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 🛠️ Step 1: Import Dependencies & Create Multimodal Synthetic Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "We build a custom PyTorch `Dataset` that generates paired samples of:\n",
    "- **Image Feature Vectors** ($\mathbf{x}_{img} \in \mathbb{R}^{64}$)\n",
    "- **Text Embeddings** ($\mathbf{x}_{text} \in \mathbb{R}^{128}$)\n",
    "- **Target Class Label** ($y \in \{0, 1\}$) computed from non-linear interaction between image and text features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "import torch.optim as optim\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set seeds for reproducibility\n",
    "torch.manual_seed(42)\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "class MultimodalSyntheticDataset(Dataset):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Custom PyTorch Dataset producing aligned Image & Text feature vectors.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    def __init__(self, num_samples=800, img_dim=64, text_dim=128):\n",
    "        self.img_data = torch.randn(num_samples, img_dim)    # 800 image feature vectors\n",
    "        self.text_data = torch.randn(num_samples, text_dim)  # 800 text embedding vectors\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Non-linear cross-modal target label generation\n",
    "        # Label is 1 if top features of image + top features of text > 0 else 0\n",
    "        interaction = (self.img_data[:, :5].sum(dim=1) * 0.6 + self.text_data[:, :5].sum(dim=1) * 0.4)\n",
    "        self.labels = (interaction > 0).long()\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def __len__(self):\n",
    "        return len(self.labels)\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n",
    "        return self.img_data[idx], self.text_data[idx], self.labels[idx]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Split dataset into Train (80%) and Test (20%)\n",
    "full_dataset = MultimodalSyntheticDataset(num_samples=1000)\n",
    "train_size = int(0.8 * len(full_dataset))\n",
    "test_size = len(full_dataset) - train_size\n",
    "train_dataset, test_dataset = torch.utils.data.random_split(full_dataset, [train_size, test_size])\n",
    "\n",
    "train_loader = DataLoader(train_dataset, batch_size=32, shuffle=True)\n",
    "test_loader = DataLoader(test_dataset, batch_size=32, shuffle=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"📊 Dataset Loaded: {len(train_dataset)} Train Samples, {len(test_dataset)} Test Samples.\")\n",
    "img_sample, text_sample, label_sample = train_dataset[0]\n",
    "print(f\"🔹 Image Tensor Shape: {img_sample.shape} | Text Tensor Shape: {text_sample.shape} | Target Label: {label_sample.item()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 🔹 Step 2: Build 3 Core Multimodal Fusion Architectures in PyTorch\n",
    "\n",
    "We implement and compare the 3 fundamental paradigm models:\n",
    "1. **EarlyFusionNet**: Concatenates raw input features before passing through a single deep neural network.\n",
    "2. **LateFusionNet**: Uses separate sub-network encoders for Image and Text modalities, then fuses their bottleneck latent embeddings.\n",
    "3. **CrossAttentionFusionNet**: Uses Transformer Multihead Cross-Attention (`nn.MultiheadAttention`) to dynamically query image features using text context."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ==========================================\n",
    "# 1️⃣ EARLY FUSION ARCHITECTURE\n",
    "# ==========================================\n",
    "class EarlyFusionNet(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, img_dim=64, text_dim=128, hidden_dim=64, num_classes=2):\n",
    "        super(EarlyFusionNet, self).__init__()\n",
    "        # Fuse directly at input layer (img_dim + text_dim = 192)\n",
    "        self.classifier = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Linear(img_dim + text_dim, hidden_dim * 2),\n",
    "            nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden_dim * 2),\n",
    "            nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.Dropout(0.3),\n",
    "            nn.Linear(hidden_dim * 2, hidden_dim),\n",
    "            nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.Linear(hidden_dim, num_classes)\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def forward(self, img_x, text_x):\n",
    "        # Concatenate raw inputs\n",
    "        fused_input = torch.cat((img_x, text_x), dim=1)\n",
    "        return self.classifier(fused_input)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ==========================================\n",
    "# 2️⃣ LATE FUSION ARCHITECTURE\n",
    "# ==========================================\n",
    "class LateFusionNet(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, img_dim=64, text_dim=128, hidden_dim=64, num_classes=2):\n",
    "        super(LateFusionNet, self).__init__()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Modality Encoder 1: Vision Sub-Network\n",
    "        self.img_encoder = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Linear(img_dim, hidden_dim),\n",
    "            nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden_dim),\n",
    "            nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.Dropout(0.2)\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Modality Encoder 2: Language Sub-Network\n",
    "        self.text_encoder = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Linear(text_dim, hidden_dim),\n",
    "            nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden_dim),\n",
    "            nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.Dropout(0.2)\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Joint Multimodal Classifier Layer\n",
    "        self.fusion_classifier = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Linear(hidden_dim * 2, hidden_dim),\n",
    "            nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.Linear(hidden_dim, num_classes)\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def forward(self, img_x, text_x):\n",
    "        img_feat = self.img_encoder(img_x)\n",
    "        text_feat = self.text_encoder(text_x)\n",
    "        # Concatenate latent representations\n",
    "        fused_features = torch.cat((img_feat, text_feat), dim=1)\n",
    "        return self.fusion_classifier(fused_features)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ==========================================\n",
    "# 3️⃣ CROSS-ATTENTION FUSION ARCHITECTURE\n",
    "# ==========================================\n",
    "class CrossAttentionFusionNet(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, img_dim=64, text_dim=128, embed_dim=64, num_heads=4, num_classes=2):\n",
    "        super(CrossAttentionFusionNet, self).__init__()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Linear projections to common embedding dimension\n",
    "        self.img_proj = nn.Linear(img_dim, embed_dim)\n",
    "        self.text_proj = nn.Linear(text_dim, embed_dim)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Multihead Cross-Attention Layer (Query=Text, Key=Image, Value=Image)\n",
    "        self.cross_attn = nn.MultiheadAttention(embed_dim=embed_dim, num_heads=num_heads, batch_first=True)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        self.classifier = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Linear(embed_dim * 2, embed_dim),\n",
    "            nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.Linear(embed_dim, num_classes)\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def forward(self, img_x, text_x):\n",
    "        # Project modalities to embed_dim -> [batch, 1, embed_dim]\n",
    "        img_emb = self.img_proj(img_x).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "        text_emb = self.text_proj(text_x).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Cross Attention: Text queries Image keys/values\n",
    "        attn_out, _ = self.cross_attn(query=text_emb, key=img_emb, value=img_emb)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Squeeze sequence dimension and concatenate with projected text\n",
    "        attn_out = attn_out.squeeze(1)\n",
    "        text_emb = text_emb.squeeze(1)\n",
    "        fused = torch.cat((attn_out, text_emb), dim=1)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        return self.classifier(fused)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ All 3 Multimodal Architectures Successfully Defined!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 🔹 Step 3: General Training & Evaluation Engine\n",
    "\n",
    "We define a modular PyTorch training loop that optimizes model parameters over 25 epochs using **Cross-Entropy Loss** and the **Adam Optimizer**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def train_and_evaluate(model, train_loader, test_loader, epochs=25, lr=0.003):\n",
    "    criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n",
    "    optimizer = optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=lr)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    history = {'train_loss': [], 'train_acc': [], 'test_acc': []}\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for epoch in range(epochs):\n",
    "        # Training phase\n",
    "        model.train()\n",
    "        running_loss = 0.0\n",
    "        correct = 0\n",
    "        total = 0\n",
    "        \n",
    "        for imgs, texts, labels in train_loader:\n",
    "            optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
    "            outputs = model(imgs, texts)\n",
    "            loss = criterion(outputs, labels)\n",
    "            loss.backward()\n",
    "            optimizer.step()\n",
    "            \n",
    "            running_loss += loss.item() * imgs.size(0)\n",
    "            _, preds = torch.max(outputs, 1)\n",
    "            correct += (preds == labels).sum().item()\n",
    "            total += labels.size(0)\n",
    "            \n",
    "        epoch_loss = running_loss / total\n",
    "        epoch_acc = correct / total\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Evaluation phase\n",
    "        model.eval()\n",
    "        test_correct = 0\n",
    "        test_total = 0\n",
    "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "            for imgs, texts, labels in test_loader:\n",
    "                outputs = model(imgs, texts)\n",
    "                _, preds = torch.max(outputs, 1)\n",
    "                test_correct += (preds == labels).sum().item()\n",
    "                test_total += labels.size(0)\n",
    "                \n",
    "        test_acc = test_correct / test_total\n",
    "        \n",
    "        history['train_loss'].append(epoch_loss)\n",
    "        history['train_acc'].append(epoch_acc)\n",
    "        history['test_acc'].append(test_acc)\n",
    "        \n",
    "    return history\n",
    "\n",
    "# Train all 3 Models\n",
    "print(\"🏋️ Training Model 1: Early Fusion...\")\n",
    "early_model = EarlyFusionNet()\n",
    "early_hist = train_and_evaluate(early_model, train_loader, test_loader)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🏋️ Training Model 2: Late Fusion...\")\n",
    "late_model = LateFusionNet()\n",
    "late_hist = train_and_evaluate(late_model, train_loader, test_loader)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🏋️ Training Model 3: Cross-Attention Fusion...\")\n",
    "attn_model = CrossAttentionFusionNet()\n",
    "attn_hist = train_and_evaluate(attn_model, train_loader, test_loader)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🎉 All Models Trained Successfully!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 🔹 Step 4: Visualizing Performance Comparison & Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "We plot convergence curves comparing Training Loss and Test Accuracy across Early, Late, and Cross-Attention Fusion strategies."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "epochs_range = range(1, 26)\n",
    "fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot Loss Decay\n",
    "ax1.plot(epochs_range, early_hist['train_loss'], 'r--', label='Early Fusion')\n",
    "ax1.plot(epochs_range, late_hist['train_loss'], 'b-', label='Late Fusion')\n",
    "ax1.plot(epochs_range, attn_hist['train_loss'], 'g-.', label='Cross-Attention Fusion')\n",
    "ax1.set_title(\"Training Loss Decay Comparison\")\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel(\"Epoch\")\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel(\"Loss\")\n",
    "ax1.grid(True)\n",
    "ax1.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot Test Accuracy\n",
    "ax2.plot(epochs_range, [a * 100 for a in early_hist['test_acc']], 'r--', label='Early Fusion')\n",
    "ax2.plot(epochs_range, [a * 100 for a in late_hist['test_acc']], 'b-', label='Late Fusion')\n",
    "ax2.plot(epochs_range, [a * 100 for a in attn_hist['test_acc']], 'g-.', label='Cross-Attention Fusion')\n",
    "ax2.set_title(\"Test Accuracy Comparison (%)\")\n",
    "ax2.set_xlabel(\"Epoch\")\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel(\"Accuracy (%)\")\n",
    "ax2.grid(True)\n",
    "ax2.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"🏆 Final Test Accuracies:\")\n",
    "print(f\"   - Early Fusion:           {early_hist['test_acc'][-1]*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"   - Late Fusion:            {late_hist['test_acc'][-1]*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"   - Cross-Attention Fusion: {attn_hist['test_acc'][-1]*100:.2f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 🔮 Step 5: Practical Inference on New Data\n",
    "\n",
    "Here is how to pass a single new pair of Image Feature Vector and Text Embedding through our trained Late Fusion model to predict class output."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def predict_multimodal_sample(model, image_vec, text_vec):\n",
    "    model.eval()\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        # Ensure batch dimension is present [1, feature_dim]\n",
    "        if image_vec.dim() == 1:\n",
    "            image_vec = image_vec.unsqueeze(0)\n",
    "        if text_vec.dim() == 1:\n",
    "            text_vec = text_vec.unsqueeze(0)\n",
    "            \n",
    "        output = model(image_vec, text_vec)\n",
    "        probabilities = torch.softmax(output, dim=1)\n",
    "        predicted_class = torch.argmax(probabilities, dim=1).item()\n",
    "        confidence = probabilities[0][predicted_class].item()\n",
    "        \n",
    "    return predicted_class, confidence\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate sample test input\n",
    "sample_img = torch.randn(1, 64)\n",
    "sample_text = torch.randn(1, 128)\n",
    "\n",
    "pred_class, conf = predict_multimodal_sample(late_model, sample_img, sample_text)\n",
    "print(f\"🔍 Prediction Result: Class {pred_class} (Confidence: {conf*100:.2f}%)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 🎯 Summary & Real-World Key Takeaways\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Modality Representation**: Vision encoders (CNNs/ViTs) convert pixels into dense spatial feature vectors, while Language encoders (BERT/Transformers) convert tokens into contextual embeddings.\n",
    "2. **Fusion Selection**:\n",
    "   - **Early Fusion**: Quick setup, but susceptible to noise and dominance by one modality.\n",
    "   - **Late Fusion**: Highly modular, enables training modality encoders separately.\n",
    "   - **Cross-Attention Fusion**: State-of-the-art method used in modern LLMs (Flamingo, Gemini, BLIP-2) allowing dynamic cross-modal interaction.\n",
    "3. **Next Steps**: Try replacing synthetic vectors with real CLIP image embeddings (`clip.load(\"ViT-B/32\")`) and text embeddings!"
   ]
